---
import ContentPage from "../components/ContentPage.astro";
import { REACHES, STATIONS } from "@lontra-creek/sim";
import { RELEASE } from "../site.ts";
import { CREEK_PATH, REACH_MARKERS } from "../creek-map.ts";
const chapters = ["Dawn survey", "The creek rises", "Into Slate Canyon", "The protected holt", "Hand over the tablet", "Log a sighting"];
---
<ContentPage title="A field trip through live state" eyebrow="Lontra Creek · guided demo" description="Follow one real subscription from its first snapshot through a lost connection, an access check, and a new identity.">
  <p class="status-note">Lontra Creek, its people, and its otters are fictional. The gateway and browser SDK are real. <span data-walk-source>Connecting to the field station…</span></p>
  <div data-walkthrough>
    <nav aria-label="Walkthrough chapters" class="chapters">{chapters.map((name,i) => <a href={`#chapter-${i+1}`} data-chapter-link>{i+1}. {name}</a>)}</nav>
    <p role="status" data-walk-status>Opening your volunteer session…</p>
    <div data-walk-unavailable hidden class="status-note">The field station is unavailable. The rest of the site still works. Run this demo locally with <code>npm install</code> and <code>npm run dev</code> from <a href="https://github.com/jfricano/lontra-creek">the demo repository</a>. <button class="btn" type="button" data-walk-retry>Try again</button></div>
    <div data-idle-notice hidden class="status-note">Your session was closed after ten minutes idle or hidden. <button class="btn" type="button" data-session-resume>Resume with fresh snapshots</button></div>
    <div class="panel-grid">
      <section class="content-card" aria-label="Current chapter">
        <article data-chapter="1"><h2 tabindex="-1">1. Dawn survey</h2><p>You are a volunteer at Kestrel Bend. The gauge first authorizes, then synchronizes, receives a snapshot, and becomes live. Watch the SDK timeline below.</p></article>
        <article data-chapter="2" hidden><h2 tabindex="-1">2. The creek rises</h2><p>Every update is a full state with a newer revision. The simulation chooses its own weather; this chapter observes it.</p><p data-flow-change>Collecting readings to compare the last twelve simulation ticks…</p></article>
        <article data-chapter="3" hidden><h2 tabindex="-1">3. Into Slate Canyon</h2><p>Cut this page's connection. Your last values stay visible and become stale while the creek continues upstream.</p><button class="btn" data-walk-drop type="button" disabled>Drop my connection</button> <button class="btn" data-walk-restore type="button" disabled>Restore connection</button><p data-revision-gap></p></article>
        <article data-chapter="4" hidden><h2 tabindex="-1">4. The protected holt</h2><p>Den locations are restricted to researchers. A volunteer request is refused with no data. After chapter 5, your researcher identity has access; restart as a volunteer to repeat the denial.</p><button class="btn" data-holt-request type="button" disabled>Request Holt A</button><p data-holt-result>Not requested.</p><button class="btn" type="button" data-volunteer-restart>Restart as a volunteer</button></article>
        <article data-chapter="5" hidden><h2 tabindex="-1">5. Hand over the tablet</h2><p>The field biologist is a different subject. Changing identity closes the old subscriptions with UNAUTHENTICATED; fresh subscriptions can read the protected holt.</p><button class="btn" data-role-switch type="button" disabled>Sign in as field biologist</button><p data-role-result>Signed in as a volunteer.</p></article>
        <article data-chapter="6" hidden><h2 tabindex="-1">6. Log a sighting</h2><p>Your private notebook is written through the site API, published to Kafka, then delivered through your own subscription.</p><p data-notebook-note>Checking whether the field station uses Kafka…</p><form data-sighting-form>
          <label for="sighting-otter">Otter</label><select id="sighting-otter" name="otterId"><option value="LO-07">Pebble</option><option value="LO-03">Birch</option><option value="LO-11">Juniper</option><option value="untagged">Untagged otter</option></select>
          <label for="sighting-reach">Reach</label><select id="sighting-reach" name="reachId">{REACHES.map(r=><option value={r.id}>{r.name}</option>)}</select>
          <label for="sighting-activity">Activity</label><select id="sighting-activity" name="activity">{["resting","foraging","traveling","grooming","playing"].map(a=><option>{a}</option>)}</select>
          <button class="btn primary" type="submit" disabled data-sighting-submit>Log sighting</button>
        </form><ol data-notebook-entries></ol></article>
        <nav class="chapter-controls" aria-label="Chapter navigation"><button class="btn" data-chapter-back type="button">Back</button><span data-chapter-count>1 of 6</span><button class="btn primary" data-chapter-next type="button">Next</button></nav>
        <details class="chapter-events" open>
          <summary>Live SDK events</summary>
          <ol tabindex="0" data-walk-log aria-label="SDK state timeline"></ol>
          <p>The public SDK exposes revisions and snapshots; the timeline reports only events received by this browser.</p>
        </details>
      </section>
      <section class="content-card" aria-labelledby="gauge-title"><h2 id="gauge-title">Kestrel Bend · LC-02</h2><p>Subscription <strong data-walk-state>idle</strong></p><dl class="gauge-values"><div><dt>Flow</dt><dd><span data-walk-flow>—</span> cfs</dd></div><div><dt>Water</dt><dd><span data-walk-temp>—</span> °C</dd></div><div><dt>Revision</dt><dd data-walk-revision>—</dd></div><div><dt>Snapshot count</dt><dd data-walk-epoch>0</dd></div></dl><p>Snapshot count labels observed synchronization attempts; it is not the gateway's internal epoch ID.</p>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 520 310" role="img" aria-label="Schematic of the fictional 14.2 kilometre Lontra Creek, with four gauge stations." class="creek-map"><path d={CREEK_PATH} fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="8"/>{REACH_MARKERS.map(marker=><g><circle cx={marker.x} cy={marker.y} r="5" fill="var(--ink)"/><text x={marker.labelX} y={marker.labelY} text-anchor={marker.anchor} font-size="12" fill="var(--ink)">{marker.name}</text></g>)}</svg>
        <ul>{STATIONS.map(station=><li>{station.id} · {station.name}</li>)}</ul><p data-map-holt hidden></p>
      </section>
    </div>
    <details class="content-card walkthrough-code" open><summary>Under the hood · walkthrough code</summary><pre tabindex="0"><code data-chapter-code></code></pre></details>
  </div>
  <aside class="content-card walk-next" aria-labelledby="walk-next-title" data-walk-next>
    <h2 id="walk-next-title">After the walkthrough</h2>
    <p>The walkthrough never breaks the shared creek. To see what a bad reading does, borrow your own bench in the Failure Lab: Fouled sensor pauses LC-03 at the record, and the gateway retries that same record after a repair.</p>
    <p><a class="btn primary" href="/lab/?scenario=fouled-sensor#source-failures">Next: handle a bad reading</a></p>
    <p class="muted">This demo runs <code>streamotter@{RELEASE}</code>. Quarantine and guarded continuation are planned for StreamOtter V1.1 and aren't in this release.</p>
  </aside>
</ContentPage>
<script>import "../scripts/walkthrough.ts";</script>
<style>
/* Each panel follows its content rather than stretching to its taller neighbour. */
.panel-grid { align-items:start; }
.chapter-events { margin-top:28px; padding-top:20px; border-top:1px solid var(--line); }
.walkthrough-code { margin-top:24px; }
.walk-next { margin-top:24px; } .walk-next .btn { text-decoration:none; }
.chapters { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:8px 20px; margin-block:24px; } .chapters a[aria-current] { font-weight:800; text-decoration-thickness:3px; }
.chapter-controls { display:flex; gap:12px; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; margin-top:28px; }
.gauge-values { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:20px; } .gauge-values dd { margin:4px 0; font-family:var(--mono); overflow-wrap:anywhere; }
.creek-map { width:100%; } [data-walk-log] { max-height:240px; overflow:auto; overflow-wrap:anywhere; font: .8rem/1.6 var(--mono); }
[data-walk-state="stale"] { color:var(--stale); } form button { margin-top:20px; }
</style>
